  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Copy (command $0b, from the command table at $0d74). The user marks a rectangle. Then a frame of the same size follows the cursor, and a press copies the rectangle there; this repeats. The source is the picture copy at $8000 (copy_source 0) or the swap picture at $e000 (copy_source 2). Source pixels with bit pair 0 are not copied. No touch and a long press ends the tool ($1495)."},
    {"at":3,"placement":"side","text":"Keeps current_colour in zoom_pixel_x ($79) until the end."},
    {"at":10,"placement":"side","text":"Script $2f5f through $0dd0: the picture with the tool label."},
    {"at":17,"placement":"side","text":"tool_colour = current_colour; the frame uses the background colour."},
    {"at":25,"placement":"side","text":"$1168 and $2793 give the first corner in shape_x0/shape_y0. $1359 and $1200 move the frame to the second corner (point_x1/point_y1) until a press."},
    {"at":65,"placement":"side","text":"copy_source_x0: the left edge of the source."},
    {"at":94,"placement":"side","text":"copy_width and copy_height of the rectangle."},
    {"at":111,"placement":"side","text":"Copy after Swap: shows the other picture."},
    {"at":122,"placement":"line","text":"Waits for the target: a touch moves the frame, a press copies, no touch and a long press ends the tool."},
    {"at":151,"placement":"line","text":"The frame starts at the cursor point. Its end is the start plus copy_width and copy_height, at most $9f and $c7."},
    {"at":200,"placement":"line","text":"End of Copy: removes the frame and sets current_colour again. After a copy from the swap picture, it swaps the pictures back and starts the copy again."},
    {"at":224,"placement":"line","text":"Copies the rectangle: first copy_clear_target, then for each pixel of the target (point_x0-point_x1, point_y0-point_y1) the pixel of the source (copy_source_x, copy_source_y) with its colour."},
    {"at":253,"placement":"side","text":"A = source_byte, X = source_pair_index; $18ec gives the bit pair."},
    {"at":263,"placement":"side","text":"copy_bit_pair: 1-3."},
    {"at":265,"placement":"side","text":"source_screen_ptr = row * 40 + column: the offset of the source cell."},
    {"at":312,"placement":"side","text":"Adds the base of the source colours: $d000/$d400 or $d800/$dc00."},
    {"at":333,"placement":"side","text":"Reads the colour byte of the source cell into current_colour (screen byte for bit pairs 1 and 2, colour RAM for 3)."},
    {"at":340,"placement":"side","text":"Bit pair 1: the high nybble of the screen byte."},
    {"at":360,"placement":"side","text":"Bit pair for current_colour in the target cell, then writes it."},
    {"at":397,"placement":"line","text":"For each pixel of the target rectangle whose source pixel is not bit pair 0, writes bit pair 0 to the target pixel."},
    {"at":399,"placement":"side","text":"Nothing in the program reads $4f6d."},
    {"at":479,"placement":"line","text":"Draws the frame point_x0/point_y0 - point_x1/point_y1 with the XOR plot ($1359): a second call removes it. Keeps cursor_x and cursor_y."},
    {"at":495,"placement":"line","text":"Jumps to read_source_pixel."},
    {"at":523,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the source byte of the pixel (X, Y) of the Copy source: the bitmap row address from the table at $1979, plus the base of copy_source_bitmap_offsets ($8000 or $e000), plus Y and 7, plus the cell column. The read ($4364) switches I/O and ROM off. Output: A = source_byte, X = source_pair_index (4 - (X and 3)) for $18ec."},
    {"at":641,"placement":"line","text":"Added to the high byte of the bitmap row address, index copy_source: 0 = $20 ($8000), 2 = $80 ($e000)."},
    {"at":644,"placement":"line","text":"2 bytes for each copy_source (0 and 2): the high byte of the source screen colours ($d0, $d8), then the distance to the source colour RAM ($04)."}
  ],
